{ "data": { "text": "Images were preprocessed using SPM12 … Artifact Detection Tool (ART) was used for outlier detection … CompCor method was applied … Residual BOLD timeseries was detrended linearly and band-pass filtered (0.008–0.09 Hz).\n\nA connectivity matrix was generated for each subject and each REST condition by calculating the correlation coefficient between 32 ROIs included in the CONN toolbox. These 32 ROIs span across eight networks: the default-mode network (DMN), the sensorimotor network (SMN), the visual network (VN), the salience network (SN), the dorsal attention network (DAN), the frontoparietal/central executive network (CEN), the language networks (LN), and the cerebellar network (CN).\n\nThree types of graph theoretical measures were computed for each subject and for each REST condition: functional integration (global efficiency and average path length), functional segregation (clustering coefficient and local efficiency), and centrality (degree and betweenness centrality). Following recommendations, for every ROI, these six measures were calculated adopting a conventional 2-sided p-value corrected using the Bonferroni correction for multiple comparisons to identify statistically significant correlations between ROIs and a two-sided cost value of 0.15 as adjacency matrix threshold for network edges." }, "annotations": [ { "result": [ { "from_name": "Time series ROI", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 25, "end": 30, "text": "SPM12", "labels": ["Time series ROI — Software"] } }, { "from_name": "Time series ROI", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 66, "end": 69, "text": "ART", "labels": ["Time series ROI — Software"] } }, { "from_name": "Time series ROI", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 101, "end": 108, "text": "CompCor", "labels": ["Time series ROI — Algorithm/Type"] } }, { "from_name": "Time series ROI", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 155, "end": 176,